    "mover": "Blue SSK",
    "mast": "uhf",
    "dwell_min": 10,
    "step_min": 30,
    "layers": 6,
    "radius_km": 20,
    "note": "Worked exposure (sub-surface): UHF mast up for 10 minutes at 26 dBm (power turned down from the 40 dBm profile) within 20 km of the boat, half-hourly layers over three hours. While the MPA is on station its ESM hears the mast anywhere in the area; in its gap (T+60 to T+120) the water to the north-east, furthest from the ships' ESM, opens. At the full 40 dBm no window opens. Try the periscope and HF masts too. Choose the forecast and run first for sea clutter.",
    "eirp_dbm": 26
  },
